{"id":"trauer","lemma":"Trauer","pos":"noun","rank":2648,"glosses":["grief, sorrow","mourning"],"ipa":"/ˈtʁaʊ̯ɐ/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/8d/De-Trauer.ogg/De-Trauer.ogg.mp3","gender":"f","forms":{"genitive":"Trauer"},"examples":[{"text":"Wir sind in Trauer.","en":"We're in mourning.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"are","l":"sein"},{"g":"in"},null]},{"text":"Er wäre beinahe vor Trauer verrückt geworden.","en":"He was so sad that he almost went mad.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"to be","l":"sein"},{"g":"almost"},{"g":"in front of, ahead of"},null,{"g":"crazy, mad"},{"g":"become, got"}]},{"text":"Der Tod des Präsidenten war Anlass großer Trauer.","en":"The president's death caused great sorrow.","words":[{"g":"the"},{"g":"death"},{"g":"of the","l":"der"},{"g":"president","l":"Präsident"},{"g":"was","l":"sein"},{"g":"cause"},{"g":"big","l":"groß"},null]},{"text":"Krieg wird von Elend und Trauer begleitet.","en":"Misery and sorrow accompany war.","words":[{"g":"war, warfare"},{"g":"to become","l":"werden"},{"g":"from / of"},{"g":"miserable"},{"g":"and"},null,{"g":"to accompany","l":"begleiten"}]},{"text":"Keine Worte können ihre tiefe Trauer lindern.","en":"No words can relieve her deep sorrow.","words":[{"g":"no / not a","l":"kein"},{"g":"word as an isolated unit","l":"Wort"},{"g":"can, to be able to"},{"g":"her","l":"ihr"},{"g":"depth"},null,{"g":"to alleviate"}]}]}